 # Existing JSON utility
 
-Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Existing action: field_names. Domain functions accept the payload object; api.dispatch routes it. CLI reports ValueError/KeyError with stderr and exit 2.
+Use `python cli.py` with one JSON object on stdin. Actions:
+
+- `field_names`: payload `{"action":"field_names","fields":{...}}` → sorted list of keys.
+- `encode`: payload `{"action":"encode","fields":{"k":"v",...}}` → log line string.
+  Keys must match ASCII `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*` (invalid keys raise `ValueError`).
+  Fields are emitted in sorted key order, tab-separated as `key=value`.
+  In values: `\` → `\\`, TAB → `\t`, LF → `\n`, CR → `\r`; all other characters
+  (including `=` and Unicode) are left as-is. Empty fields encode to `""`.
+- `decode`: payload `{"action":"decode","line":"..."}` → object mapping keys to string values.
+  Splits on literal TAB, then on the FIRST `=` only. Unescapes exactly `\\`, `\t`,
+  `\n`, `\r`; unknown or trailing backslash escapes raise `ValueError`.
+  Empty line decodes to `{}`. Invalid keys, duplicate keys, empty fields
+  (including a trailing TAB), or fields without `=` raise `ValueError`.
+
+Domain functions accept the payload object; `api.dispatch` routes it. CLI reports
+`ValueError`/`KeyError` on stderr with exit code 2 (no traceback) and prints the
+JSON result on success. Inputs are never mutated, including rejected ones.
+
+Regression tests: `python -B -m unittest tests/test_domain.py`.
